3. SHAPE-SHIFTING SYSTEM
================================================================================

Inspired by LocoRoco's shape-changing mechanic, lots and data elements can
transform based on context or data state.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.1 Default State
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

All lots and primary data objects appear as circular blobs at rest. The circle
represents completeness, neutrality, and the organic nature of coffee as an
agricultural product.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.2 Contextual Transformation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Certain views or data states trigger shape transformation:

TRANSFORMATION TRIGGERS
- Entering a specific view (e.g., cupping suite transforms blobs to squares)
- Data state change (e.g., flagged lot becomes triangular)
- User preference (e.g., "structured view" renders all as squares)

TRANSFORMATION BEHAVIOR
- Morph animation: 300-400ms ease-in-out
- Shape persists within context
- Returns to default (circle) when exiting context
- Transformation should feel like the blob is being gently pressed into a mold

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.3 Shape Semantic Mapping
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CIRCLE (default)
- Standard lot representation
- Complete data sets (Black Circle/ Type changes to white)
- Neutral/unreviewed status (White Circle / Type is black)

SQUARE
- Processed or structured data view (Reading Square is White/ Type is black)
- User input (Square remains white/ Type remains black / But there's a black dashes outline)
- Verified/confirmed information
- Cupping data and scores
- Export documentation

TRIANGLE
- Alerts or flags requiring attention
- Incomplete data (missing stages)
- Discrepancies between reported and verified data
- Urgent items in inventory

IMPLEMENTATION NOTE
Shape is a CSS/SVG property, not a component swap. Use border-radius
manipulation and clip-path for smooth morphing:

  circle:    border-radius: 50%
  square:    border-radius: 8-12px (slightly rounded corners)
  triangle:  clip-path: polygon(50% 0%, 0% 100%, 100% 100%)

