4. GROWTH AND AGGREGATION MECHANIC
================================================================================

Inspired by LocoRoco eating berries to grow, lots visually expand as they
accumulate data, verifications, or transaction history. A circular outline rests
in the background when lot is in its standard representaion, suggesting the space
that can be filled with further data input; i.e. a filled circle is ideally complete.
This can be related to the visibility score (section 5) but a growth metric is provided
at the moment.  

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.1 Growth Representation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DATA RICHNESS AS SIZE
- Minimum size: lot with only basic identification (origin, ID)
- Maximum size: fully documented lot with complete chain of custody

GROWTH INCREMENTS
- Each major data category adds one "unit" of growth
- Maximum of 20 units (matching LocoRoco's cap)
- Visual size scales logarithmically (early growth more noticeable)

DATA CATEGORIES CONTRIBUTING TO GROWTH (1 unit each)
1. Farm/producer identification
2. Geographic coordinates
3. Altitude documentation
4. Varietal specification
5. Harvest date range
6. Processing method
7. Drying method
8. Moisture content reading
9. Export documentation
10. Shipping/logistics data
11. Import documentation
12. Warehouse/storage data
13. Sample roast data
14. Cupping score (official)
15. Cupping score (user-submitted)
16. Roast profile data
17. Retail/distribution data
18. End consumer feedback
19. Certifications (organic, fair trade, etc.)
20. Media/photos attached

SIZE CALCULATION
  growthUnits = count of populated data categories (0-20)
  visualScale = 1 + (growthUnits * 0.05)  // ranges from 1.0 to 2.0
  
  Minimum diameter: 48px
  Maximum diameter: 96px

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.2 Split and Merge Interactions
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SPLIT (tap)
- Single tap on a lot blob splits it into individual data points
- Each data point becomes its own mini-blob
- Mini-blobs arrange in a cluster or grid
- Useful for examining specific stages or comparing components

MERGE (hold)
- Press and hold on split view
- Individual blobs animate toward center
- Coalesce into single summary blob
- Returns to default lot view

FORCED SPLIT POINTS
- Entering detailed stage view forces split
- Cupping comparison view shows split scores
- Discrepancy review shows conflicting data as separate blobs

ANIMATION TIMING
- Split: 400ms staggered (each blob pops out sequentially)
- Merge: 600ms convergent (all blobs move simultaneously to center)

