5. VISIBILITY SCORE SYSTEM
================================================================================

The visibility score quantifies supply chain transparency based on data
contributed by participants at each stage.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.1 Purpose and Definition
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Visibility Score: a 0-100 metric indicating how well-documented a lot's journey
is from farm to cup.

- 0-25: Opaque (minimal documentation)
- 26-50: Partial (some stages documented)
- 51-75: Transparent (most stages documented with verification)
- 76-100: Fully Visible (complete documentation, multiple verifications)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.2 Calculation Methodology
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

BASE SCORE (max 60 points)
Each supply chain stage contributes points when documented:

  Stage                     Points
  ----------------------------------------
  Farm/Producer             8
  Harvest                   6
  Processing                8
  Drying                    6
  Milling                   4
  Export                    8
  Shipping                  6
  Import                    6
  Warehousing               4
  Roasting                  4
  ----------------------------------------
  Total possible:           60

VERIFICATION BONUS (max 20 points)
Third-party or cross-referenced verification adds points:

  Verification Type         Points
  ----------------------------------------
  Certification body        5
  Lab analysis              5
  Multiple participant
    confirmation            5
  Photographic evidence     3
  GPS/timestamp data        2
  ----------------------------------------
  Total possible:           20

RECENCY BONUS (max 10 points)
Data updated within relevant timeframes:

  Update Recency            Points
  ----------------------------------------
  Within 30 days            10
  Within 90 days            7
  Within 180 days           4
  Within 1 year             2
  Older than 1 year         0
  ----------------------------------------

PARTICIPANT DIVERSITY BONUS (max 10 points)
Number of unique participants contributing data:

  Participants              Points
  ----------------------------------------
  5+ participants           10
  4 participants            8
  3 participants            6
  2 participants            4
  1 participant             2
  ----------------------------------------

FINAL CALCULATION
  visibilityScore = baseScore + verificationBonus + recencyBonus + diversityBonus
  visibilityScore = clamp(visibilityScore, 0, 100)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.3 Visual Representation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Since color is prohibited, visibility manifests through form properties:

OPACITY/SOLIDITY
- High visibility (76-100): solid black fill, crisp edges
- Good visibility (51-75): solid black fill, slight softness
- Partial visibility (26-50): 70% opacity, softer edges
- Low visibility (0-25): 40% opacity, diffuse/fuzzy edges

EDGE TREATMENT
- High visibility: clean, defined border (2px solid)
- Decreasing visibility: increasingly wobbly/unstable border animation

OPTIONAL: INTERNAL TEXTURE
- High visibility: solid fill
- Lower visibility: internal noise or stipple pattern suggesting uncertainty

NUMERIC DISPLAY
- Score displayed as integer (0-100) on tap or in detail view
- Positioned below or beside the lot blob
- Typography: 600 weight, same typeface as system

