8. GLOBAL VIEW
================================================================================

The Global View shows a lot's relationships to other lots in the world supply.
This feature is deferred pending database architecture decisions.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.1 Purpose
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Visualize where a lot fits in the broader coffee supply network
- Show connections: same origin, same importer, same roaster, etc.
- Enable discovery of related lots

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.2 Dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Before implementation, the following must be defined:

DATABASE ARCHITECTURE
- Lot-to-lot relationship schema
- Participant (producer, exporter, importer, roaster) entity model
- Geographic hierarchy (country → region → farm)

RELATIONSHIP TYPES
- Geographic proximity (same region, neighboring farms)
- Supply chain overlap (same exporter, same importer)
- Quality similarity (similar cupping profiles)
- Temporal proximity (same harvest season)

NETWORK QUERY PATTERNS
- "Show all lots from this producer"
- "Show all lots handled by this importer"
- "Show lots with similar cupping profiles"

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.3 Placeholder Implementation
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Until full network visualization is built:

SIMPLE RADIAL VIEW
- Central blob: current lot
- Surrounding blobs: related lots (limited to 6-8)
- Connecting lines indicate relationship type
- Line thickness indicates strength of relationship

RELATIONSHIP LABELS
- Tap connecting line to see relationship type
- Tap related lot to navigate to its timeline

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.4 Future Visualization Concepts
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

GEOGRAPHIC MAP
- World map with origin regions as blob clusters
- Drill down: country → region → farm
- Lots represented as small blobs within regions

SUPPLY CHAIN FLOW
- Sankey-style diagram showing lot movement
- Width indicates volume
- Participants as nodes

SIMILARITY CONSTELLATION
- Lots positioned by cupping profile similarity
- Closer blobs = more similar flavor profiles
- Interactive: drag to reposition, pinch to zoom

