9. TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS
================================================================================

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.1 Platform Targets
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

PRIMARY: Mobile Web (Progressive Web App)
- iOS Safari
- Android Chrome
- Responsive: 320px - 428px viewport width


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.2 Technology Stack (Recommended)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

FRONTEND
- Framework: React 18+ with TypeScript
- Animation: Framer Motion (physics-based springs)
- Styling: CSS Modules or Tailwind CSS (grayscale config)
- State: Zustand or React Context (lightweight)
- Gestures: react-use-gesture or native touch events

BUILD TOOLING
- Vite (fast development, optimized builds)
- TypeScript strict mode
- ESLint + Prettier

BACKEND (Future)
- API: Node.js with Express or Fastify
- Database: PostgreSQL (relational data) + optional graph DB for network
- Authentication: OAuth 2.0 (Google, Apple sign-in)
- Hosting: Vercel (frontend), Railway or Render (backend)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.3 Animation Specifications
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SPRING CONFIGURATIONS (Framer Motion syntax)

Default squish (button press):
{
  type: "spring",
  stiffness: 400,
  damping: 17
}

Blob wobble (idle):
{
  type: "spring",
  stiffness: 100,
  damping: 10,
  mass: 1
}

Page transition:
{
  type: "spring",
  stiffness: 300,
  damping: 30
}

Split animation:
{
  type: "spring",
  stiffness: 200,
  damping: 20,
  staggerChildren: 0.05
}

Merge animation:
{
  type: "spring",
  stiffness: 150,
  damping: 25
}

SQUISH BEHAVIOR

On press:
- Scale X: 1.1
- Scale Y: 0.9
- Duration: 100ms to squished state

On release:
- Return to scale 1.0
- Spring physics for overshoot and settle
- Total settle time: ~300ms

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.4 Gesture Handling
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SWIPE DETECTION
- Minimum distance: 50px
- Maximum duration: 300ms
- Angle tolerance: 30° from cardinal direction

SWIPE RESPONSE
- Elastic resistance at boundaries (no content beyond)
- Momentum: velocity-based animation distance
- Snap threshold: 30% of screen width/height

TOUCH FEEDBACK
- Immediate visual response on touch start (<16ms)
- Squish begins on touch, completes on release
- No delay for tap detection

